msgid "Scene:Color:Decal"
msgstr "Place an image"

msgid "Help:Decal"
msgstr "Applies an image inside this edit's range. Turn on 'Place with a box' in Settings to project it straight from a box instead. While on, the color, shading, opacity and gradient settings apply to the image, not to the range. Drag the image in the Scene to slide it along the surface (a sticker keeps facing the surface). Use the small window next to the panel to show or hide the handles."

msgid "Scene:Color:DecalStickerCaption"
msgstr "Places the image like a sticker where you clicked. Drag the image to move it, use the corners to resize and the ring to rotate."

msgid "Scene:Color:DecalBoxMode"
msgstr "Place with a box"

msgid "Help:DecalPlacement"
msgstr "When on, the image is projected straight from the front of a box (parallel projection) instead of being laid along the surface like a sticker. Use the box gizmo and face handles to set the depth, width and height, flipping and direction in detail. Useful to fill a whole part such as a tie, or to span separate parts. Each edit remembers this (a new image starts with it off). Turning it off keeps the image size, moves its center onto the surface and turns it to face the surface. To select the image again, click anywhere inside its frame when off, or on a non-transparent part when on. The 'Image' button in the small window next to the panel shows or hides the handles."

msgid "Scene:Color:DecalBoxCaption"
msgstr "The image is projected straight from the front of the teal box onto the surfaces inside it."

msgid "Scene:Color:DecalFollowSurface"
msgstr "Also turn to the surface"

msgid "Help:DecalFollowSurface"
msgstr "When on, dragging the image also turns the box to face the surface under the cursor. When off, the box keeps its projection direction and only moves (to slide it while still projecting from the front). Only for placing with a box."

msgid "Scene:Color:DecalSmooth"
msgstr "Place smoothly (lilToon/Poiyomi)"

msgid "Help:DecalSmooth"
msgstr "On shows the image directly on an overlaid mesh instead of baking it into the texture. Edges stay smooth, and you can place it on just one side of clothes whose left and right share UVs. Works with lilToon and unlocked Poiyomi materials."

msgid "Scene:Color:DecalSmoothUnavailable"
msgstr "Materials other than lilToon/Poiyomi (including locked Poiyomi) get the image baked in"

msgid "Scene:Color:DecalNormal"
msgstr "Apply normal map"

msgid "Help:DecalNormal"
msgstr "When on, the original material's normal map is remapped to the image position and used on the overlaid surface, so the fabric's wrinkles and shading also appear on the image. The 2nd normal map (such as fabric weave) is kept as is, unless it uses UV1. This adds one normal-map texture (sized to match the original normal map's detail). Does nothing if the original material has no normal map. Poiyomi uses the clothing's own normal maps directly, so no texture is added."

msgid "Scene:Color:DecalKeepAspect"
msgstr "Keep aspect ratio"

msgid "Help:DecalKeepAspect"
msgstr "On keeps the image's aspect ratio inside the box. Off stretches it to fill the box's XY."

msgid "Scene:Color:GradientPreview"
msgstr "Color 1 → Color 2"

msgid "Scene:Color:EditTarget:Start"
msgstr "Color 1"

msgid "Scene:Color:EditTarget:End"
msgstr "Color 2"

msgid "Scene:Color:Padding"
msgstr "Edge padding"

msgid "Scene:Color:DeleteEdit"
msgstr "Delete this edit"

msgid "Scene:Label:Format"
msgstr "{0} / {1} / {2}"

msgid "Help:ShowRange"
msgstr "Overlays stripes in the Scene on the area the current edit recolors. This does not affect the uploaded result."

msgid "Help:PerSeedStats"
msgstr "When on, the brightness distribution is taken separately for each part added with Ctrl+Click, and each one is matched to the target color. When off, one distribution is taken for the whole selection, so brightness differences between parts are kept. The same applies to links across materials."

msgid "Help:Mode"
msgstr "Decides how much gets recolored when you click. Changing it also updates the edit you are working on."

msgid "Help:Mode:Island"
msgstr "Part: recolors the whole part (UV island) you clicked."

msgid "Help:Mode:SameColor"
msgstr "Same color: recolors only colors that nearly match the clicked spot. Good for patterns and lines."

msgid "Help:Mode:SimilarColor"
msgstr "Similar color: recolors a wider range of colors close to the clicked spot. Good for gradients and shaded areas."

msgid "Scene:Panel:Mode:Box"
msgstr "Inside box"

msgid "Help:Mode:Box"
msgstr "Inside box: recolors only what is inside the box shown in the Scene. The cut follows the box faces regardless of parts or UV seams. Move the box with its handles."

msgid "Scene:Select:BoxFeather"
msgstr "Face softness"

msgid "Help:BoxFeather"
msgstr "How softly the recolor fades out at the box faces. 0 gives a hard cut."

msgid "Scene:Select:BoxPerPartStats"
msgstr "Match colors inside box"

msgid "Help:BoxPerPartStats"
msgstr "When on, the brightness distribution is taken separately for each part (UV island) inside the box and each one is matched to the target color, like Match color per point with several parts selected. When off, one distribution is taken for the whole box, so brightness differences between parts are kept."

msgid "Help:Threshold"
msgstr "How close a color has to be to get selected. Higher selects more, lower selects less."

msgid "Help:Feather"
msgstr "Softens the edge of the selection. Higher values blend the border more gradually."

msgid "Help:Scope"
msgstr "Where to look for matching colors.\nConnected: only the area that connects to the clicked spot without a break\nWithin part: only inside the clicked part\nWhole texture: anywhere in the same texture\nWhole avatar: every texture on the avatar (this can be slow)"

msgid "Help:Cleanup"
msgstr "Removes small scattered dots that the texture's paint leaves in the selection. Higher values also remove larger dots."

msgid "Help:DarkEnd"
msgstr "How dark the shaded areas become. Right makes shadows darker, left makes them lighter. Move it left if shadows look grayish with bright colors such as white."

msgid "Help:ShadingStretch"
msgstr "Areas with weak original shading (such as nearly pure white or black hair) keep weak shading after recoloring and can look flat. Raising the value stretches the shading to fill the whole target brightness range (too high also makes the original noise more visible). Combine it with 'Match color per point' to give multiple parts the same tone and the same shading."

msgid "Scene:Color:FlattenBase"
msgstr "Cancel original gradient (experimental)"

msgid "Scene:Color:FlattenStrength"
msgstr "Strength"

msgid "Help:FlattenBase"
msgstr "Removes the light-dark difference of the original color (e.g. roots to tips) so the whole area matches. Works top to bottom (along the gradient box when Gradient is on). Shading is kept. Lower the strength if it looks too flat."

msgid "Help:Strength"
msgstr "Opacity of the recolor. At 1 the chosen color is applied fully; lower values keep more of the original color."

msgid "Help:Gradient"
msgstr "When on, a box appears in the Scene. The color changes from Color 1 at the bottom of the box to Color 2 at the top. Move the box to set the direction and range. Use the small window next to the panel to show or hide the box."

msgid "Help:GradientInsideOnly"
msgstr "When on, everything above the top and below the bottom of the box is left as the original color, and only the box height becomes a gradient. Sideways the box does not cut anything. When off, the colors continue beyond both ends."

msgid "Help:Padding"
msgstr "How far (in pixels) the color spreads into unused texture space around the part. Raise it if a line of the original color shows along seams. Negative values shrink the selection edge instead."

msgid "Help:PreviewResolution"
msgstr "Maximum resolution used for the Scene preview. Lower is faster. Upload and export always use the original resolution."

msgid "Help:ApplyOnBuild"
msgstr "When on, your edits are baked into the main texture on upload (build) in the paid edition. The original textures and materials are left unchanged. The trial edition only shows a notice in the report window."

msgid "Help:Export:Main"
msgstr "Saves a new texture with your edits baked in (name_recolor.png) next to the original. With 'Duplicate and replace materials' on, the materials are duplicated and swapped in. Exported edits are turned off automatically. Ctrl+Z undoes it."

msgid "Help:Export:Second"
msgstr "Puts only the recolored area on lilToon's 2nd layer (or the 3rd if the 2nd is in use). The main texture stays as it is, so turning the layer off brings back the original. Exported edits are turned off. A warning is shown if the 3rd layer is also in use. Ctrl+Z undoes it."

msgid "Help:Export:Mask"
msgstr "Saves the selection as a black-and-white image (name_recolormask.png) that you can use as a mask in other tools. Materials and edits are not changed."

msgid "Help:Export:CropSecond"
msgstr "Crops the 2nd-layer image to just the area around the selection so the file stays small. The layer position is adjusted automatically."

msgid "Error:SeedRendererMissing"
msgstr "The Renderer clicked for edit '{0}' was not found (it may have been deleted), so this edit is skipped."

msgid "Error:TextureUnused"
msgstr "Texture '{0}' is not used by any material on the avatar, so it is skipped."

msgid "Error:ComputeUnavailable"
msgstr "Compute shaders are not available in this environment, so recoloring cannot be applied on upload."

msgid "Error:MaskFailed"
msgstr "Could not build the selection for edit '{0}' (for example, mesh Read/Write is disabled or the GPU is unavailable), so this edit is skipped."

msgid "Error:ApplyFailed"
msgstr "Could not apply recoloring to texture '{0}', so it is skipped."

msgid "Error:ProOutdated"
msgstr "The paid edition is outdated, so images placed with 'Place smoothly' are not applied on upload. Please update the paid edition."

msgid "Error:ProOutdatedHair"
msgstr "The paid edition is outdated, so recolors on Chimera Hair Master hair are not uploaded as previewed. Please update the paid edition."

msgid "Error:ChmMergedHair"
msgstr "Texture '{0}' is used by Chimera Hair Master hair with mesh merging ON, so the recolor is not applied to that hair."

msgid "Error:ChmHairSlotMismatch"
msgstr "The material count of '{0}' changed during the build, so the recolor over Chimera Hair Master is not applied."

msgid "Error:FreeEdition"
msgstr "Trial edition: not applied on upload (available in the paid edition)."

msgid "Error:OriginalTextureStillReferenced"
msgstr "Original texture '{0}' is still referenced (material '{1}'), so both the original and the generated texture will be included in the upload."

msgid "Error:OverlayMeshUnreadable"
msgstr "Mesh '{0}' has Read/Write disabled, so the smoothly placed image is not applied. Enable Read/Write in the mesh's import settings."

msgid "Error:OverlayTooFewMaterials"
msgstr "'{0}' has fewer materials than submeshes, so the smoothly placed image is not applied."

msgid "Error:OverlayImageFailed"
msgstr "Could not create the image for edit '{0}' (for example, the GPU is unavailable), so this edit's image is skipped."

msgid "Error:OverlayMaterialFailed"
msgstr "Could not create the overlay material for '{0}', so the image of edit '{1}' is not applied to this Renderer."

msgid "Error:OverlayApplyFailed"
msgstr "Could not apply the smoothly placed image to '{0}' (see the Console for details)."
